  "articleBody": "Ever wonder what a general contractor really does on a remodeling project? It's more than just swinging a hammer, that's for sure! At its core, a general contractor is your go-to person for coordinating everything. They kick things off by defining the project’s scope with you, then move on to estimating costs and sequencing all the different trades – like plumbing and electrical – that will be involved. Getting permits, if needed, is also on their plate, as is scheduling inspections to keep everything on track and up to code. Throughout the project, they manage progress, handle payments to subcontractors, and oversee the closeout process. This means they’re making sure everyone is doing their part, that materials arrive on time, and that the work meets quality standards. They’re also your main point of contact, making sure you’re updated on the schedule and how things are progressing. It’s all about making your remodeling journey as smooth as possible by handling the complexities behind the scenes. If you’re planning a multi-trade project or anything structural, having a solid general contractor is a game-changer.",
